<title>SINGAPORE: Parkway 1st-half net profit up 55 pct.</title>
<headline>Parkway 1st-half net profit up 55 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 23.49 vs   15.11</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	     8.08 vs    5.31</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (percent)    5.00 vs    5.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			  193.43 vs   92.47</p>
<p>    Investment income		 0.42 vs    0.49</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest   9.49 vs    9.86</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)	     22.83 vs   13.77</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization    13.79 vs    2.98</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	 5.66 vs    6.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   31.79 vs   20.25</p>
<p>    Tax				   8.43 vs    5.10</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (gain) 0.12 vs    0.03 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  (gain) 0.68 vs    4.89 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Parkway Holdings Ltd is a property and healthcare company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
